        "",
        "## 3. Test 20: Up-Quark Hierarchy ($m_u : m_c : m_t$) and Top–Bottom Scale Ratio $\\tan\\beta(M_Z) = \\lvert A_5 \\rvert = 60$",
        "",
        "1. **Top-to-Bottom Scale Ratio $\\tan\\beta(M_Z) = \\lvert 2I / Z(2I) \\rvert = \\lvert A_5 \\rvert = 60$:**",
        "   At $\\mu = M_Z$, the running top-to-bottom mass ratio equals the order of the bosonic icosahedral rotation group $2I / Z(2I) \\cong A_5$ ($\\lvert A_5 \\rvert = 60$):",
        f"   $$\\tan\\beta(M_Z)_{{\\text{{exp}}}} = \\frac{{m_t(M_Z)}}{{m_b(M_Z)}} = \\frac{{171.7 \\pm 1.5\\text{{ GeV}}}}{{2.85 \\pm 0.03\\text{{ GeV}}}} = \\mathbf{{{phase5.exp_tan_beta_mz:.2f} \\pm 0.80}} \\;\\longleftrightarrow\\; \\lvert A_5 \\rvert = \\mathbf{{{phase5.pred_tan_beta_mz:.2f}}} \\quad (\\mathbf{{{phase5.tan_beta_rel_err_pct:.2f}\\% = 0.3\\sigma}}\\text{{ match!}}).$$",
        "2. **Quadratic Clock Scaling in the $q_{\\text{PQ}} = 0$ Up-Quark Sector ($m_c / m_t = (m_\\mu / m_\\tau)^2$):**",
        "   Because $H_u = (\\Sigma[4], \\text{PQ}[0])$ carries $q_{\\text{PQ}} = 0$ (unlike $H_d = H_e = (\\Sigma[3], \\text{PQ}[-1])$, which carries $q_{\\text{PQ}} = -1$), the up-quark mass matrix is quadratic in the Clock Yukawa operator ($Y_u \\propto Y_e^2$):",
        f"   - **Charm-to-Top Ratio at $M_Z$:** $\\left(\\frac{{m_c}}{{m_t}}\\right)_{{M_Z}}^{{\\text{{pred}}}} = \\left(\\frac{{m_\\mu}}{{m_\\tau}}\\right)_{{M_Z}}^2 = \\mathbf{{{phase5.pred_mc_over_mt_mz:.6f}}} = \\frac{{1}}{{282.8}}$ vs. $\\left(\\frac{{m_c}}{{m_t}}\\right)_{{M_Z}}^{{\\text{{exp}}}} = \\mathbf{{{phase5.exp_mc_over_mt_mz:.6f}}} = \\frac{{1}}{{277.4}}$, predicting $m_c(M_Z) = \\mathbf{{{phase5.pred_mc_mz_gev:.3f}\\text{{ GeV}}}}$ vs. exp `{phase5.exp_mc_mz_gev:.3f} ± 0.017 GeV` (**1.9% error, $0.7\\sigma$**).",
        f"   - **Up-to-Charm Ratio at $M_Z$:** Including the single-color $N_c^{{-1}} = 1/3$ suppression, $\\left(\\frac{{m_u}}{{m_c}}\\right)_{{M_Z}}^{{\\text{{pred}}}} = \\frac{{1}}{{3}}\\frac{{m_e}}{{m_\\mu}} = \\mathbf{{{phase5.pred_mu_over_mc_mz:.5f}}}$ vs. exp `{phase5.exp_mu_over_mc_mz:.5f}`, predicting $m_u(M_Z) = \\mathbf{{{phase5.pred_mu_mz_mev:.2f}\\text{{ MeV}}}}$ vs. exp `{phase5.exp_mu_mz_mev:.2f} ± 0.19 MeV` (**$1.4\\sigma$**).",
        "",
